Description:
In this lab, you will explore how Kubernetes Services enable network communication between pods and abstract away the underlying pod IPs.

You will create a simple nginx Deployment, scale it to multiple replicas, and expose it using a ClusterIP Service. By doing this, you’ll learn how Kubernetes automatically load-balances traffic across all the pods that match a Service’s selector.

This lab demonstrates the basic working of Service discovery in Kubernetes — how Services find and route to Pods using labels and selectors, and how Endpoints maintain this mapping dynamically as pods are added or removed.

Objective:
Understand the role of Kubernetes Services in exposing applications.

Learn how to link Deployments and Services using label selectors.

Observe how Endpoints map to pods and verify Service-to-Pod communication.

Tasks:
Verify that the namespace svc-lab exists.

Create a Deployment named web-deploy using the nginx image.

Scale the Deployment to 3 replicas.

Expose the Deployment as a Service named web-service on port 80 (ClusterIP).

Verify that:

The Service exists and has a valid ClusterIP.

Endpoints show 3 pod IPs corresponding to the replicas.

