Check existing namespaces:
kubectl get namespaces

→ Confirms if svc-lab namespace exists.

Create deployment in svc-lab namespace:
kubectl -n svc-lab create deployment web-deploy --image=nginx

→ Creates a Deployment named web-deploy running nginx containers.

Scale deployment to 3 replicas:
kubectl -n svc-lab scale deployment web-deploy --replicas=3

→ Ensures three pods are running for load balancing.

Expose deployment as a Service:
kubectl -n svc-lab expose deployment web-deploy --port=80 --target-port=80 --name=web-service

→ Creates a Service that forwards requests on port 80 to backend pods.

Verify Service creation:
kubectl -n svc-lab get svc web-service

→ Checks Service type (ClusterIP) and assigned ClusterIP address.

Check Endpoints mapping:
kubectl -n svc-lab get endpoints web-service

→ Ensures the Service is correctly routing to all pod IPs (3 in total).

Verify pods and labels:
kubectl -n svc-lab get pods -l app=web-deploy

→ Confirms that the label selector matches Service configuration (important for endpoints).


